Mapping
  curation.csv, one row per Book, in file order
    dsp_id                             iri, as http://rdfh.ch/0803/<dsp_id>
    id                                 slug
    date_display                       date_display@de
    office, title_override, sort_key   the same key
    cover_page (a pages.csv id)        cover_page, as that Page's IRI
    teaser_de, teaser_en               teaser@de, teaser@en
  annotation-curation.csv, one row per Region or LinkObj, in file order
    id                                 iri, as http://rdfh.ch/0803/<id>
    keep, lang, name                   the same key
    note                               #note, a comment column, never served
    kind                               dropped: it restates the resource's class
  translate.py, the last row, the Band http://rdfh.ch/0803/EJZQcYisXECHxchG_KQ27w
    UNSIGNED_STRIP_ID                  slug
    UNSIGNED_STRIP_NAME                name

pages.csv has no IRI column. A Page's IRI is http://rdfh.ch/0803/ followed by the last path segment of
its ark cell, without the check digit (the last character) and with every = turned into -. Every value
is copied verbatim.

The file was derived once, by a script that is not kept, and is edited by hand from then on: it is not
regenerated. Since dsp-incubator#500 (DEV-7496, merged 2026-10-10) it is the only copy of
Incunabula's curation: the incubator deleted the source files above and builds its store from this
file, which it vendors. A curation change is made here and reaches the incubator when it re-vendors.

Every row names a resource of areas/access/sync/data/0803.nq. If a regenerated 0803.nq drops one, CPE
leaves Incunabula not ready until the row is removed or re-keyed by hand.

